# target: a DECLARE LIBRARY of a prebuilt Windows .a, which Linux's lookup does not find (libv37c.a).
v37_f_static	target: `DECLARE LIBRARY` of a prebuilt library; Linux's lookup says LIBRARY not found
v37_h_customtype	target: `DECLARE LIBRARY` of a prebuilt library; Linux's lookup says LIBRARY not found
v37_x68	target: `DECLARE LIBRARY` of a prebuilt library; Linux's lookup says LIBRARY not found
# float: _FLOAT is IEEE quad precision in wasm32 (DIVERGENCES-QB64PE.md D-069).
v30_a_using_numbers	float: PRINT USING of a _FLOAT 1/3 shows quad precision's digits (D-069)
v58_f01_hyperbolic	float: _ARCTANH of a _FLOAT is .5493061443340548, x87's .549306144334055 (D-069)
v58_f04_atanh_const	float: _ATANH of a _FLOAT is .5493061443340548, x87's .549306144334055 (D-069)
# float: a float converted to an integer outside its range saturates in WebAssembly (D-071).
v20_d_val	float: VAL of 1e30 to an _INTEGER64 is 9223372036854775807, x86-64's -9223372036854775808 (D-071)
v20_f_math_edges	float: _ROUND(1E30) is -1, x86-64's -9223372036854775808 (D-071)
v33_c06_system_2_pow_40	float: SYSTEM 2 ^ 40 exits with 255, x86-64's 0 (D-071)
# clib: musl's math (D-070).
v22_f_functions	clib: _TANH(.5!) is .4621171355247498, glibc's .4621171653270721 (D-070)
# width: what this target is, a 32-bit one that is not Linux (spec compiler/wasm-target, "The target's name").
v16_m6_conditions	width: $IF 32BIT is true and $IF LINUX false, so another branch prints
v16_m6_error_inactive	width: $IF LINUX is false, so its $ERROR is inactive and the program builds
v16_m6_inactive_header	width: $IF LINUX is false, so its unclosed IF is inactive and the program builds
v49_c_md5_os	width: _OS$ is [WASM][32BIT], Linux's [LINUX][64BIT]
v18_d_index_big	width: the index 4294967296 wraps to 0 in a 32-bit ptrszint, so no error 9
v20_i_on_goto	width: ON n GOTO with n = 4294967298 takes n in 32 bits and falls through, no error 5
v63_g2_reassign_large_string	width: two strings of 1.1 GB do not fit in wasm32's 4 GB: Out of memory (D-066)
v63_g3_concat_over_2gb	width: strings of 1.2 GB do not fit in wasm32's 4 GB: Out of memory before line 3
# width: a pointer is 4 bytes (OpenSpec change wasm-pointer-width; spec compiler/wasm-target, "A pointer is 4
# bytes on this target"). The recordings are QB64pe's 64-bit build.
v21_a_decls	width: an _UNSIGNED _OFFSET of -1 is 4294967295, LEN of an _OFFSET is 4, and a 64-bit literal is cut to 32 bits
v21_a_functions	width: a FUNCTION AS _UNSIGNED _OFFSET returns -1 as 4294967295
v21_a_suffixes	width: a ~%& variable of -1 is 4294967295 and its LEN is 4
v21_b_float_stores	width: 1.8D+19 stored in an _OFFSET keeps its low 32 bits, 3305635840
v21_b_passing	width: an _INTEGER64 passed to an _OFFSET parameter is copied, not passed by reference, so the caller keeps its value
v21_d_builtins	width: STR$, HEX$, OCT$, _BIN$ and ABS of an _UNSIGNED _OFFSET of -1 show 32 bits
v21_d_for	width: a FOR over a ~%& ends at 4294967295
v21_e_scenarios	width: an _OFFSET member makes the TYPE 20 bytes, and an _INTEGER64 passed to an _OFFSET parameter is copied
v21_g_passing_places	width: an _INTEGER64 member or element passed to an _OFFSET parameter is copied, so it is unchanged after
v24_a_define	width: LEN of a variable made _OFFSET by _DEFINE is 4
v24_x179_param_offset_to_integer64	width: an _INTEGER64 array is not the storage of an _OFFSET array parameter: a compile error
v30_d_binary	width: a record with an _OFFSET is 4 bytes shorter, so LOF is 64
v32_c_mk_cv	width: _MK$ of an _OFFSET is 4 bytes and _CV of one reads 4; also _MK$ of a _FLOAT is quad precision's bytes (D-069)
v35_x22_mem_of_variable	width: ELEMENTSIZE of the _MEM of an _OFFSET is 4
v35_x52_layout_offsets	width: a dynamic member array's slot is 4 bytes, so the TYPE is 12 bytes and its members' offsets halve
v48_d_len_whole	width: LEN of a whole _OFFSET array of 2 elements is 8
v48_x11_mem_type_string_member	width: SIZE of the _MEM of a TYPE with STRING members is 32
v48_x30_len_whole_string_member_array	width: LEN of a whole member array of 4 strings is 16
v49_a_cast	width: _CAST to _OFFSET keeps 32 bits: 4294967295 becomes -1
v56_a1_scalar_offsets	width: the _OFFSET variables take 4 bytes of the conventional memory, so VARPTR of each is 4 or 8 higher
v56_b1_varptr_dollar_numbers	width: VARPTR$ of an _OFFSET has the type byte 20, and the addresses are 4 higher
v56_g1_len_string_member_arrays	width: LEN of a member array of strings counts 4 bytes for each
v56_g2_mem_string_member_types	width: SIZE and ELEMENTSIZE of a _MEM over STRING members count 4 bytes for each
v61_a2_types	width: the _OFFSET variables take 4 bytes of the conventional memory, so VARPTR of each is 4 or 8 higher
v62_h1_cast_variables	width: _CAST to _OFFSET and _UNSIGNED _OFFSET keeps 32 bits: 3000000000 becomes -1294967296
